1. Files derived from aleph-alpha-inference
-------------------------------------------

aleph-alpha-inference 1.0.0, the vLLM plugin that serves Kolibri 1
  Copyright 2026 Aleph Alpha GmbH
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  Source: https://github.com/Aleph-Alpha/aleph-alpha-inference
  Commit: 049a6a7bd2405b27d6d280d256bd3d585191c7ae

The following files are derived works of that source. Each carries an
"SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0" header and a line stating that it was
modified for MLX/numpy by Miktam for Chronos exp_036 on 2026-10-03.

  port/kolibri1.py
      MLX re-implementation of aleph_alpha_inference/kolibri1.py (the
      Kolibri1 attention, routing, MoE block and decoder layer) for mlx_lm.
      convert.py copies this file, unchanged, into every converted model
      directory, so it is distributed with each converted checkpoint.

  reference/kolibri_ref.py
      Independent float32 numpy re-implementation of the same forward pass,
      including the vendor's sigmoid_logit_add_routing.

  reference/mutants.py
      The seven G3 reference mutants (HYPOTHESIS Phase 0, G3): subclasses of
      the numpy reference, each re-expressing one plausible misreading of the
      vendor's Kolibri1 forward pass (routing, RoPE, RMSNorm, norm order).

  gate/port_mutants.py
      The 15 port mutants of HYPOTHESIS Phase 0: patches of a fresh copy of
      port/kolibri1.py's module that re-express parts of the Kolibri1
      attention, router and MoE code in deliberately wrong variants.
      port/kolibri1.py itself is never edited.

  tests/tiny_checkpoint.py
      numpy re-expression of the vendor's tests/checkpoints.py (tiny random
      checkpoint with the real tensor names and the vendor test config).

  tests/test_routing.py
      numpy re-expression of the vendor's test_routing_semantics from
      tests/test_kolibri1.py.

Modifications: the code was rewritten from PyTorch/vLLM to MLX (port) and
numpy (reference, mutants, tests). aleph-alpha-inference ships no NOTICE file
of its own.


